<section class="section" aria-labelledby="about-coll-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="seo-copy">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h2 id="about-coll-{{ section.id }}">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
        <div class="seo-copy__body">{{ section.settings.text }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection about",
  "class": "section dews-collection-about",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "About the cane collection"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Content",
      "default": "<p>Cane furniture earned its reputation the hard way. Woven rattan has been used in furniture making for well over two centuries because it does something no solid panel can: it carries weight while staying light, and it breathes, so a chair back stays cool to lean against on a warm afternoon.<\/p><p>Every cane panel in this collection is woven by hand and set into a routed groove in the frame — the traditional method.<\/p><h3>Choosing the right piece<\/h3><ul><li><strong>For a small living room<\/strong> — the Heritage 2-Seater or the Dark Cane Bench Sofa.<\/li><li><strong>For a reading corner<\/strong> — the Cane &amp; Rattan Accent Chair.<\/li><li><strong>For a bedroom refresh<\/strong> — the Cane Headboard pairs with an existing base.<\/li><li><strong>For storage that isn't bulky<\/strong> — the cane-front sideboards.<\/li><\/ul><h3>Caring for cane<\/h3><p>Cane wants humidity. In a very dry room it can become brittle over years, so keep pieces away from a radiator or a direct heating vent.<\/p>"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Collection about"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
